# 21. A new term I think we should add: admissible observable

This may become the bridge between the entire programme and the source.

Define provisionally:

$$
\boxed{
\mathcal O_{\rm adm}(Q,\Gamma)
}
$$

as the family of observations that are admissible for inquiry \(Q\) in context \(\Gamma\).

Then:

$$
s_1\equiv_{\mathcal O_{\rm adm}}s_2
$$

means:

> the two states are indistinguishable under all admissible observations.

That gives us a very clean chain:

$$
Q,\Gamma
$$

$$
\downarrow
$$

$$
\mathcal R_{\rm req}
$$

$$
\downarrow
$$

$$
\mathcal O_{\rm adm}
$$

$$
\downarrow
$$

$$
\equiv_{\mathcal O}
$$

$$
\downarrow
$$

$$
S/\equiv_{\mathcal O}.
$$

This could become a major part of the D1 → D4 bridge.

