# 26. Most important correction to our previous work

I would therefore revise our earlier conclusion:

### Previous

> "Topology may provide a mathematical foundation for KnowledgeOS."

### New

> **Topology is one candidate mathematical structure that may emerge if KnowledgeOS requires notions of neighbourhood, convergence, continuity or closure. Before introducing topology, KnowledgeOS should define the more primitive concepts of admissible observation, separation, observational equivalence, quotient, congruence and structural minimality.**

That is much more consistent with our methodology.

The source gives us evidence that **families of mappings can generate a weakest structure and, when sufficiently separating, a faithful representation**.  But that does not establish that KnowledgeOS itself has such a structure.

